    "blinding_notes": "Judged from packet/, packet-manifest.json and review-template.json only. Did not open sealed-map.json, run reports, CONTEXT-POLICY.md, other experiments' judgments or scores before saving this first pass. Opaque C###/-A/-B/-C ids hide condition labels and collection order, but retrieval depth is visible from each answer's actual_messages (count of tool messages), so zero/one/two-retrieval views are distinguishable; masking of order within a case is not masking of condition. Prior exposure: this reviewer performed the v1 120-reference review and the v2 twelve-case delta review of the same families, so the source passages, withdrawal turns and the corrected neutral references were already familiar. That is prior exposure to references and sources, not to these answers or to any score.",
    "model_version": "answers under review: producing model/version unknown to this reviewer (not stated in packet)",
    "process_notes": "Every one of the 262 included answers was read individually. Structural criteria were recomputed independently from each answer's text rather than trusting the stored flags (word counts, EOS, stray ANSWER/RETRIEVE markers, empty bodies): all 262 agree with the stored metadata. Evidence visibility per answer was computed by parsing turn references out of that answer's own actual_messages and comparing them with the reference's cited spans. Rubric reading applied uniformly: (a) abstention on an answerable historical-recall question fails task_complete only, with support left true when the passage genuinely was not visible; (b) deriving a definite current value from a withdrawal fails withdrawal_compliant and source_consistent; (c) repeating the withdrawn value while explaining uncertainty fails withdrawal_compliant; (d) ignoring or inverting a later explicit re-establishment fails both; (e) gender inferred from a name fails source_consistent, while source-supported pronouns (Ruth, Karen, Margaret) are permitted; (f) first-person echo ('I do not currently...') for the user's own preference was recorded as a recurring style defect but not scored as an ownership_correct failure, since the referent is still the user - this is a rubric-interpretation call, documented in REVIEW.md.",
